From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance <livi@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] giscanner: do not merge pkg-config stderr into its output

Buildroot puts its own pkg-config in PATH, and that wrapper is a /bin/sh
script that runs with HOST_DIR/lib on LD_LIBRARY_PATH. On a build host whose
/bin/sh is bash (linked against readline, linked against the system
libncursesw), the loader prints

    /.../host/lib/libncursesw.so.6: no version information available
    (required by /usr/lib/libreadline.so.8)

on stderr as soon as the wrapper starts. check_output() merged stderr into
the pkg-config output, shlex.split() turned the warning words into linker
arguments, and the introspection dumper died with "linker input file not
found: no". The warning is noise: drop stderr instead of merging it.
---
 giscanner/pkgconfig.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/giscanner/pkgconfig.py b/giscanner/pkgconfig.py
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/giscanner/pkgconfig.py
+++ b/giscanner/pkgconfig.py
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ def check_output(flags, ignore_errors, command=None):
     argv = command[:]
     argv.extend(flags)
     try:
-        return subprocess.check_output(argv, universal_newlines=True, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
+        return subprocess.check_output(argv, universal_newlines=True, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
     except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:
         output = e.output or ''
         if ignore_errors:
-- 
